So for any set of 4 vertices {a, b, c, d}, there is a way to partition them into 2 pairs such that each pair is connected by an edge. The possible partitions are:
- {a,b} and {c,d}
- {a,c} and {b,d}
- {a,d} and {b,c}

Actually, the 3 perfect matchings on 4 vertices {a,b,c,d} are:
M1 = {ab, cd}
M2 = {ac, bd}  
M3 = {ad, bc}

Let me re-examine. The 6 edges on 4 vertices {a,b,c,d} are: ab, ac, ad, bc, bd, cd.
The 3 perfect matchings are:
M1 = {ab, cd}
M2 = {ac, bd}
M3 = {ad, bc}
